\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"1. Vegas Itinerary — Living Plan and Cash Flow — September 2026\",\"startIndex\":496,\"endIndex\":559,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"   - Master hotel calendar, hold-recycling assumptions, pinch points, fallback rules, food/liquidity treatment, and post-Vegas branches.\",\"startIndex\":560,\"endIndex\":696,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"2. 2026-09-07 — Vegas Budget, Loyalty, and Offer Strategy — Live Update\",\"startIndex\":697,\"endIndex\":768,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"   - MGM/VIP strategy, current-offer logic, Excalibur/Vdara rhythm, liquidity allocation, and loyalty/parachute doctrine.\",\"startIndex\":769,\"endIndex\":890,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"3. 2026-09-07 — Personal Operations Handoff — Budget, Vegas, Mexico, Action Items\",\"startIndex\":891,\"endIndex\":972,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"   - Cross-domain operational handoff tying Vegas budget to travel, Mexico, work, and immediate actions.\",\"startIndex\":973,\"endIndex\":1077,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"4. Vegas Food, Exercise, and Daily Rhythm — Living Plan\",\"startIndex\":1078,\"endIndex\":1133,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"   - Food/credit/grocery and daily-rhythm support.\",\"startIndex\":1134,\"endIndex\":1184,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"5. Post-Vegas Travel Options — Living Plan\",\"startIndex\":1185,\"endIndex\":1227,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"   - Florida/Mexico/later-hotel branch logic.\",\"startIndex\":1228,\"endIndex\":1273,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"OPERATING PRINCIPLES\",\"startIndex\":1275,\"endIndex\":1295,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Continuous lodging, food, phone/work connectivity, and interview/job-search capability outrank entertainment or aspirational hotel moves.\",\"startIndex\":1296,\"endIndex\":1435,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Hotel authorizations/holds are locked liquidity, not spendable cash.\",\"startIndex\":1436,\"endIndex\":1506,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Never count a checkout hold as available until it has actually posted back.\",\"startIndex\":1507,\"endIndex\":1584,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Free play is budget value $0 until converted and cashed.\",\"startIndex\":1585,\"endIndex\":1643,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Promised payments, unemployment, refunds, credits, or job income are $0 until actually posted and usable.\",\"startIndex\":1644,\"endIndex\":1751,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Keep hotel folios as close to zero as practical unless a true resort/food credit is covering the charge.\",\"startIndex\":1752,\"endIndex\":1858,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Use the cheapest safe hotel bridge when a high-end hold would endanger cash flow.\",\"startIndex\":1859,\"endIndex\":1942,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- MGM/Hard Rock status is an option portfolio/parachute, not a gambling-income strategy.\",\"startIndex\":1943,\"endIndex\":2031,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Preserve earned hotel/food/free-play value without chasing status with survival cash.\",\"startIndex\":2032,\"endIndex\":2119,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Exact current liquid cash must be refreshed from actual account balances; do not back-solve it from old snapshots.\",\"startIndex\":2120,\"endIndex\":2236,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"HOTEL / VEGAS TIMELINE — PRESERVED STATE\",\"startIndex\":2238,\"endIndex\":2278,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"Historical working sequence used through early/mid September:\",\"startIndex\":2279,\"endIndex\":2340,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Excalibur blocks were the low-cost work/bridge stays.\",\"startIndex\":2341,\"endIndex\":2396,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Vdara blocks were controlled recovery stays with larger holds and resort/free-play value.\",\"startIndex\":2397,\"endIndex\":2488,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Cosmopolitan was a higher-hold option and therefore a later liquidity pinch.\",\"startIndex\":2489,\"endIndex\":2567,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Fontainebleau was discretionary/deferrable and should never displace continuous lodging or liquidity safety.\",\"startIndex\":2568,\"endIndex\":2678,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Palms was opportunistic only when economics were favorable; prior internet/room/service issues reduced its value as a work base.\",\"startIndex\":2679,\"endIndex\":2809,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Excalibur/Luxor remained emergency MGM valves when a Vdara/Cosmo hold did not recycle in time.\",\"startIndex\":2810,\"endIndex\":2906,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"CURRENT / RECENT HOTEL STATE TO PRESERVE\",\"startIndex\":2908,\"endIndex\":2948,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Peter moved from Excalibur to New York-New York and preferred the larger corner-room setup for work: two queen beds, large windows, cool room, lots of light, room to pace/stand, fridge, and a useful TV/work surface concept.\",\"startIndex\":2949,\"endIndex\":3174,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- NY-NY became a potentially better work/value base than expected because the MGM resort credit was $300 versus a lower credit previously discussed for Cosmopolitan.\",\"startIndex\":3175,\"endIndex\":3340,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Known NY-NY eligible dining tracked in chat: Il Fornaio $54.19; Grand Wok $99.05 before tip; room service $67.55; subtotal $220.79 against the $300 resort credit, leaving an estimated $79.21 before any later adjustment. Grand Wok was considered eligible but might require manual front-desk application/reconciliation.\",\"startIndex\":3341,\"endIndex\":3660,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Non-credit room/account charges and tips were being separated from resort-credit charges rather than blended into one number.\",\"startIndex\":3661,\"endIndex\":3788,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"EXCALIBUR RELEASE / REFUND DELTAS\",\"startIndex\":3790,\"endIndex\":3823,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- $44 room-rate/prepaid-difference refund: POSTED Sunday morning, September 13.\",\"startIndex\":3824,\"endIndex\":3903,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- $55 normal incidental authorization/hold: still pending as of the latest update.\",\"startIndex\":3904,\"endIndex\":3986,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Important distinction: the $44 was an actual refund/price difference, not a hold release; the $55 is the normal pending authorization.\",\"startIndex\":3987,\"endIndex\":4123,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- This supports the standing rule that different hotel cash movements must be classified separately: refund, folio charge, deposit/authorization hold, and credit are not interchangeable.\",\"startIndex\":4124,\"endIndex\":4310,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"LIQUIDITY / CASH-FLOW MODEL\",\"startIndex\":4312,\"endIndex\":4339,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"Track every movement in one of these buckets:\",\"startIndex\":4340,\"endIndex\":4385,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"A. AVAILABLE CASH — posted and spendable now.\",\"startIndex\":4386,\"endIndex\":4431,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"B. LOCKED LIQUIDITY — hotel holds/authorizations not yet released.\",\"startIndex\":4432,\"endIndex\":4498,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"C. EXPECTED INFLOW — refund/unemployment/payment not yet posted; budget value $0 until received.\",\"startIndex\":4499,\"endIndex\":4595,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"D. NON-CASH VALUE — resort credit/free play/comp value; useful but not cash.\",\"startIndex\":4596,\"endIndex\":4672,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"E. REQUIRED OUTGO — hotel balance, phone, food, transportation, interview/work infrastructure.\",\"startIndex\":4673,\"endIndex\":4767,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"The critical question is never merely 'what is the balance?' It is:\",\"startIndex\":4769,\"endIndex\":4836,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- What is available now?\",\"startIndex\":4837,\"endIndex\":4861,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- What is locked?\",\"startIndex\":4862,\"endIndex\":4879,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- What must be paid before the next release/inflow?\",\"startIndex\":4880,\"endIndex\":4931,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- What can be deferred?\",\"startIndex\":4932,\"endIndex\":4955,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- What threatens work/interview continuity?\",\"startIndex\":4956,\"endIndex\":4999,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"PHONE / INTERNET / WORK-CONTINUITY RISK\",\"startIndex\":5001,\"endIndex\":5040,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Spectrum/mobile bill became a non-negotiable near-term risk: roughly $100 due in about two days from the Sunday-night discussion. If service is suspended, cellular data/hotspot disappears, although the phone can still use hotel Wi-Fi for Teams/Zoom.\",\"startIndex\":5041,\"endIndex\":5292,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Current hotspot performance is weak/throttled enough that it cannot safely support a 90-minute interview plus live AI/reference use on the laptop.\",\"startIndex\":5293,\"endIndex\":5441,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Phone can still serve as interview fallback over hotel Wi-Fi even if cellular service is suspended.\",\"startIndex\":5442,\"endIndex\":5543,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Laptop Wi-Fi repair is therefore mission-critical for work continuity, not just convenience.\",\"startIndex\":5544,\"endIndex\":5638,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- AX210/Wi-Fi hardware was ordered with Amazon credit and expected Tuesday, September 15. First acceptance test: install -> connect to hotel Wi-Fi -> speed test -> 10–15 minute stable stream. Do not open a tuning rabbit hole before basic function is proven.\",\"startIndex\":5639,\"endIndex\":5896,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"ANDREW / INTERVIEW CONTINUITY\",\"startIndex\":5898,\"endIndex\":5927,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Wednesday Myers-Holum final interview is the primary near-term mission.\",\"startIndex\":5928,\"endIndex\":6001,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Best case: repaired laptop Wi-Fi permits Andrew on Teams/Zoom plus prep material on a second surface.\",\"startIndex\":6002,\"endIndex\":6105,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Preferred design discovered Sunday night: do NOT depend on live AI during the interview. Externalize prep into a TV-sized command board / HTML / Word/PDF sidecar so Peter can glance, orient, and speak naturally.\",\"startIndex\":6106,\"endIndex\":6319,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Interview prep should remain usable even if cellular hotspot fails entirely.\",\"startIndex\":6320,\"endIndex\":6398,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"NY-NY WORKSPACE / DISPLAY IDEA\",\"startIndex\":6400,\"endIndex\":6430,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Use the room/TV as a large visible state surface.\",\"startIndex\":6431,\"endIndex\":6482,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Primary screen: six-lane Principal Consultant command board — Discovery -> Process -> Solution -> Delivery -> Governance -> Health / Commercial.\",\"startIndex\":6483,\"endIndex\":6629,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Secondary support: gotchas / principal-language cues.\",\"startIndex\":6630,\"endIndex\":6685,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Third/minimized layer: proof bank / resume stories.\",\"startIndex\":6686,\"endIndex\":6739,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Goal: no typing, no live note hunting, no dependency on hotspot latency during the interview.\",\"startIndex\":6740,\"endIndex\":6835,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"KNOWN HISTORICAL CASH-FLOW RULES FROM VEGAS PLAN\",\"startIndex\":6837,\"endIndex\":6885,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Earlier planning used unemployment and recycled hotel holds as the main bridge until employment income.\",\"startIndex\":6886,\"endIndex\":6991,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Excalibur clean-folio stays were used as real-world tests of hold-release timing.\",\"startIndex\":6992,\"endIndex\":7075,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Vdara/Cosmopolitan high holds were always conditional on actual prior releases posting.\",\"startIndex\":7076,\"endIndex\":7165,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Chinni/payment promises and casino free-play conversions were treated as upside only when received.\",\"startIndex\":7166,\"endIndex\":7267,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Food credits reduce cash burn but do not increase liquid cash.\",\"startIndex\":7268,\"endIndex\":7332,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Entertainment/movie decisions are allowed only when they do not endanger the next required hotel/food/work payment.\",\"startIndex\":7333,\"endIndex\":7450,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"LOYALTY / OFFER STRATEGY\",\"startIndex\":7452,\"endIndex\":7476,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- MGM Platinum should not be chased at current cash flow.\",\"startIndex\":7477,\"endIndex\":7534,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- MGM value is in existing earned offers: low-cost/comp rooms, resort credits, free play, and emergency room optionality.\",\"startIndex\":7535,\"endIndex\":7656,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Hard Rock/Unity remains the major non-MGM backup network.\",\"startIndex\":7657,\"endIndex\":7716,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Future multiplier/tier optimization belongs after normal income resumes.\",\"startIndex\":7717,\"endIndex\":7791,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Protect option value; do not convert emergency liquidity into status points.\",\"startIndex\":7792,\"endIndex\":7870,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"CHAT-CLEANUP PRESERVATION RULE\",\"startIndex\":7872,\"endIndex\":7902,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"Before deleting/cleaning old chats, preserve any new facts that change one of these categories:\",\"startIndex\":7903,\"endIndex\":7998,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"1. Actual available cash.\",\"startIndex\":7999,\"endIndex\":8024,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"2. Pending hotel holds/refunds and posted dates.\",\"startIndex\":8025,\"endIndex\":8073,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"3. Hotel reservation/check-in/check-out changes.\",\"startIndex\":8074,\"endIndex\":8122,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"4. Resort/free-play/food-credit amounts and eligibility.\",\"startIndex\":8123,\"endIndex\":8179,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"5. Phone/internet/work-continuity status.\",\"startIndex\":8180,\"endIndex\":8221,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"6. Confirmed unemployment/payment/refund inflows.\",\"startIndex\":8222,\"endIndex\":8271,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"7. Post-Vegas departure timing.\",\"startIndex\":8272,\"endIndex\":8303,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"8. Any emergency fallback that materially changes the liquidity runway.\",\"startIndex\":8304,\"endIndex\":8375,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"CURRENT OPEN ITEMS\",\"startIndex\":8377,\"endIndex\":8395,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Refresh exact current liquid cash balance from actual accounts before using any old projected number.\",\"startIndex\":8396,\"endIndex\":8499,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Confirm whether the $55 Excalibur hold has released.\",\"startIndex\":8500,\"endIndex\":8554,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Reconcile final NY-NY folio/resort-credit application after checkout.\",\"startIndex\":8555,\"endIndex\":8626,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Preserve phone service if feasible; if not, ensure hotel Wi-Fi + phone fallback remains tested.\",\"startIndex\":8627,\"endIndex\":8724,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Install/test AX210 Tuesday.\",\"startIndex\":8725,\"endIndex\":8754,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Keep Wednesday interview operational even if hotspot/cellular service is unavailable.\",\"startIndex\":8755,\"endIndex\":8842,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Re-evaluate any later Cosmo/Fontainebleau/Vegas blocks only from actual liquidity at that time, not from the old projection.\",\"startIndex\":8843,\"endIndex\":8969,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"STATUS\",\"startIndex\":8971,\"endIndex\":8977,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"Anchor created for chat cleanup. Historical Vegas/budget source docs remain intact. This file is the durable bridge between those historical planning documents and the current September 14 operating state.\",\"startIndex\":8978,\"endIndex\":9183,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"2026-09-14 — LIVE LIQUIDITY UPDATE\",\"startIndex\":9185,\"endIndex\":9219,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Checked out of New York-New York.\",\"startIndex\":9220,\"endIndex\":9255,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Pivoting to one night at Luxor.\",\"startIndex\":9256,\"endIndex\":9289,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Expected cash on hand after Luxor check-in: approximately $20.\",\"startIndex\":9290,\"endIndex\":9354,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Still waiting on the normal $55 Excalibur incidental hold to release; do not count until posted.\",\"startIndex\":9355,\"endIndex\":9453,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Possible $30 from Leon later today is upside only until received.\",\"startIndex\":9454,\"endIndex\":9521,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- Current decision read: the one-night Luxor pivot protects continuity and preserves flexibility while liquidity is tight.\",\"startIndex\":9522,\"endIndex\":9644,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"2026-09-16 — LIVE HANDOFF / CRUNCH MODEL UPDATE\",\"startIndex\":9647,\"endIndex\":9694,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- HARD AVAILABLE NOW: SoFi available balance $87.26 as of early morning Sept 16 after the prior Luxor $50 authorization released overnight. Treat this as the real starting balance; pending holds/refunds remain $0 until posted.\",\"startIndex\":9695,\"endIndex\":9921,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- PROVEN CLEAN-FOLIO DATA POINT: Luxor stay checked out online Tuesday Sept 15 with a zero/clean folio. Final folio email arrived immediately at 11:02 AM Sept 15, and the $50 authorization disappeared overnight by Sept 16. Working lesson: clean MGM folios can recycle an authorization overnight; do not generalize this to dirty/adjusted folios until repeated.\",\"startIndex\":9922,\"endIndex\":10281,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- EXCALIBUR OLD HOLD: $55.55 from the prior Excalibur stay remains pending as of Sept 16. This is the older problem hold and should not be counted.\",\"startIndex\":10282,\"endIndex\":10429,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- CURRENT EXCALIBUR HOLD: $50 from the Sept 15 Excalibur stay is pending. Peter intends to check out fully after the Myers-Holum interview today so this hold closes as its own clean transaction; then observe whether it releases overnight like Luxor.\",\"startIndex\":10430,\"endIndex\":10679,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- NY-NY: $300 authorization still pending. Final NY-NY folio was generated/sent at about 3:40 AM Sept 15 after Sept 14 checkout. Expected net release/refund remains about $160. For conservative planning, treat Friday Sept 18 as the safer availability point under the 'three full business days after closeout' rule; earlier posting is upside only.\",\"startIndex\":10680,\"endIndex\":11026,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- AMAZON: about $22 expected back around Sept 17; count only when posted.\",\"startIndex\":11027,\"endIndex\":11100,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- SILVER LIQUIDATION: Nevada Coin Mart paid $40 cash for the silver lot on Sept 15. This solved the immediate bridge. Monitor was quoted at only $10 by SuperPawn and was NOT sold; monitor remains an emergency-only lever.\",\"startIndex\":11101,\"endIndex\":11321,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- PALMS NON-CASH VALUE FOR SEPT 16: $50 dining offer and $100 free slot play are active today; three complimentary Palms room nights remain in the current offer set through Sept 30. Dining credit can carry food without touching hotel cash. Free play remains budget value $0 until converted and cashed.\",\"startIndex\":11322,\"endIndex\":11623,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- INTERVIEW CONTINUITY: Excalibur late checkout is confirmed to noon today. Myers-Holum final with Andrew is 10:00–11:30 AM, so the room protects the full interview window. After the interview, Peter plans a full checkout, not a rollover, to keep the authorization transaction clean and separately observable.\",\"startIndex\":11624,\"endIndex\":11933,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- TODAY'S ORDER: interview first -> clean Excalibur checkout -> reconcile posted balances/holds -> check back into the separately booked Excalibur stay if still needed -> then handle Thursday bridge / Luxor shuffle.\",\"startIndex\":11934,\"endIndex\":12149,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- THURSDAY BRIDGE: do not assume the old Excalibur $55.55 will arrive. Current conservative bridge depends on money actually posted plus the expected ~$22 Amazon refund. The key new upside test is whether today's clean Excalibur $50 releases overnight.\",\"startIndex\":12150,\"endIndex\":12402,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- FRIDAY / WEEKEND: Luxor reservation beginning Friday Sept 18 still needs to be shortened/reworked after the interview so the hold requirement matches actual liquidity. The expected ~$160 NY-NY release is intended to fund the weekend Luxor authorization; avoid double-counting that same $160 elsewhere.\",\"startIndex\":12403,\"endIndex\":12706,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- NEXT-WEEK BRIDGE: Excalibur Sept 21–24 remains another liquidity gate. Current strategy is to front-load / split the stay if necessary rather than fund all three nights at once. A $250 unemployment cash injection is expected around Sept 23; another separate ~$250 payment is expected around Sept 24 for the Vdara bridge. These remain $0 until posted.\",\"startIndex\":12707,\"endIndex\":13059,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- HOLD-RECYCLING RULE: every hotel hold must be earmarked to one future use only. Do not double-count recycled authorizations across Luxor, Excalibur, or Vdara.\",\"startIndex\":13060,\"endIndex\":13220,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- FOOD RULE THROUGH THE CRUNCH: use MGM/Palms dining credits before cash. Hotel/deposit cash stays isolated from food unless a specific daily reconciliation shows true slack.\",\"startIndex\":13221,\"endIndex\":13395,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- PHONE / WORK RULE: interview and laptop continuity outrank all hotel optimization. Wire/repair parts are in hand; if laptop repair still needs a store, that is an operational task after the interview, not before it.\",\"startIndex\":13396,\"endIndex\":13613,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- MAIN LESSON FROM SEPT 14–16: the problem has been timing, not total value. One-day settlement differences are material. Map exact checkout date, folio closeout time, hold amount, earmark, and earliest safe availability before committing the next stay.\",\"startIndex\":13614,\"endIndex\":13867,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"2026-09-16 — AFTERNOON HANDOFF / FINAL CASH MAP\",\"startIndex\":13868,\"endIndex\":13915,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- HARD CASH NOW: $35 available in SoFi after today’s separate Excalibur $50 authorization posted. Treat $35 as the only spendable cash unless another item actually posts.\",\"startIndex\":13916,\"endIndex\":14086,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- CURRENT PENDING HOLDS: old Excalibur $55.55 remains pending; Sept 15 Excalibur $50 remains pending; Sept 16 Excalibur $50 is now pending; NY-NY $300 remains pending. Keep each hold separate and earmarked once.\",\"startIndex\":14087,\"endIndex\":14298,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- EXCALIBUR $55.55 ESCALATION: Peter spoke with the front desk and obtained folio / authorization paperwork. If the $55.55 has not cleared by Sept 17, go downstairs and escalate with the paperwork. The folio shows $0 balance; the hold remains pending on SoFi.\",\"startIndex\":14299,\"endIndex\":14558,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- THURSDAY SEPT 17 BRIDGE: plan is one more Excalibur night at about $8 room cost plus a new $50 authorization. If the old $55.55 releases before check-in, projected hard cash after the room and new hold is about $32.55. Do not assume the release until it posts.\",\"startIndex\":14559,\"endIndex\":14821,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- FRIDAY SEPT 18 LUXOR: reservation was moved to Friday check-in for THREE NIGHTS in the Silver Tower. Working hold assumption is $50/night based on Peter’s observed Luxor one-night stay, so plan on $150 total authorization unless Luxor states otherwise at check-in. The previously floated $75/night number is discarded because it was not evidence-based.\",\"startIndex\":14822,\"endIndex\":15176,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- FRIDAY FUNDING POOL: projected bridge is about $32.55 residual cash + about $159.78 NY-NY release + about $22 Amazon refund = about $214.33 total. Against an expected $150 Luxor hold, projected remaining liquid cushion is about $64.33. Count NY-NY/Amazon only when actually posted.\",\"startIndex\":15177,\"endIndex\":15460,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- EXCALIBUR HOLD EARMARKING: the three $50 Excalibur holds generated across this Tue/Wed/Thu bridge are NOT funding Friday Luxor. They are earmarked for next week as they recycle, so they must not be double-counted in current cash.\",\"startIndex\":15461,\"endIndex\":15692,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- NEXT-WEEK LOGIC: Friday-to-Monday Luxor $150 hold should not be assumed available for Monday Sept 21 Excalibur. Continue treating the recycled Excalibur $50 holds plus Sept 23 / Sept 24 cash injections as the next-week bridge.\",\"startIndex\":15693,\"endIndex\":15921,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- PALMS VALUE: $50 dining credit and $100 free play are available today, but Peter does not need to walk to Palms in 102-degree heat just to avoid a small food spend. A roughly $5 In-N-Out burger is an acceptable cash use because current bridge math still works with a modest food spend; preserve most of the $35.\",\"startIndex\":15922,\"endIndex\":16235,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false},{\"text\":\"- HANDOFF RULE FOR NEW CHAT: carry forward the exact ledger, not broad estimates. Start from actual hard cash, list each pending hold separately, then expected inflows. Never mix pending authorizations with spendable money.\",\"startIndex\":16236,\"endIndex\":16459,\"tabId\":\"t.0\",\"namedStyleType\":\"NORMAL_TEXT\",\"isListItem\":false}],\"document_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TxQ1rANJxyyN4HT4huNslXblGP98eLOiXSUqEJkHIhA\"},\"error\":null,\"error_data\":null,\"error_code\":null,\"classification_id\":null,\"json_rpc_error_code\":null,\"error_http_status_code\":null,\"error_http_headers\":null,\"internal\":{\"external_call_time_ms\":274},\"clamp_errors\":null,\"clamp_rewrites\":null,\"connector_id\":\"connector_5f3c8c41a1e54ad7a76272c89e