ur hold, the separate $50 holds, Thursday bridge, Friday three-night Silver Tower Luxor plan with the $150 working authorization, the $214.33 projected funding pool, ~$64.33 projected cushion, and the rule that the Excalibur holds are earmarked for next week rather than Friday. fileciteturn2file0L2-L6\n\nI also updated the **Personal Operating Context Index** so a fresh personal chat now explicitly knows to use that Vegas anchor as the live source rather than reconstructing hotel math from old conversations. I added the operating rule we’ve been using too: multiple things can stay mentally active, but **one job in your hands at a time**, with the rest externalized into visible artifacts.\n\nSo this chat is clean. I understand the personal artifact structure again: **Vegas/liquidity**, **personal operating context**, **Mexico/family relocation**, **relationships/follow-ups**, and **personal systems/preferences**, while job-search material stays in its own work artifact instead of bleeding into here. fileciteturn2file4L30-L35\n\nYou shouldn’t need to re-explain the Vegas week to me from here. memcite"]}, "create_time": 1789594764.741481, "end_turn": true, "id": "cf963099-fe99-41fb-b2ba-118bd9dc0832", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 574, "metadata": {"extra": {"authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "0f040be5-d3aa-4650-bb5b-c7c8dc904eab", "cited_message_idx": 31, "cloud_doc_url": "https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TxQ1rANJxyyN4HT4huNslXblGP98eLOiXSUqEJkHIhA/edit?usp=drivesdk", "connector_id": "connector_5f3c8c41a1e54ad7a76272c89e2554fa", "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "line_range": [2, 6], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 2, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id":