page_range_start": null, "snippet": null, "source": "my_files", "start_idx": 547, "type": "file"}, {"alt": null, "cloud_doc_url": "https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ck6Q0XG_8ZSI9feHdq5AqZq298GB7M5Q4swkE9cu6RI/edit?usp=drivesdk", "connector_id": "connector_5f3c8c41a1e54ad7a76272c89e2554fa", "drug_file_reference": null, "end_idx": 1311, "fff_metadata": null, "id": "1ck6Q0XG_8ZSI9feHdq5AqZq298GB7M5Q4swkE9cu6RI", "input_pointer": {"file_index": 4, "line_range_end": 35, "line_range_start": 30, "message_id": "5c4e538e-300e-4f40-89b8-2f15a9648c77", "message_index": 2}, "library_artifact_type": null, "library_file_id": null, "matched_text": "fileciteturn2file4L30-L35", "medical_file_reference": {"authors_display": null, "doi": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "publication_year": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null}, "name": "README — Personal Operating Context Index", "page_range_end": null, "page_range_start": null, "snippet": null, "source": "my_files", "start_idx": 1282, "type": "file"}, {"alt": null, "end_idx": 1387, "invalid": false, "matched_text": "memcite", "prefix": null, "prompt_text": null, "refs": [], "safe_urls": [], "start_idx": 1378, "type": "hidden"}], "conversation_context_citation_metadata": [{"citation": {"alt": "", "attribution": "Past chat", "category": "memory", "end_idx": 0, "matched_text": "", "prompt_text": null, "pub_date": 1788881548.938564, "refs": [], "retrieval_origin": "pca", "snippet": "Absolutely. Here’s the personal-only handoff for the new chat. It deliberately excludes the AI-stack/framework work so the two lanes stay isolated.\n\nPERSONAL OPERATIONS HANDOFF — 2026-09-08 MORNING\n\nThis chat is PERSONAL OPERATIONS ONLY.\n\nDo not reopen GCE / EC⁸ architecture, AI-stack governance, scraper architecture, seat routing, model/provider design, or technical framework work unless Don explicitly brings it into this chat.\n\nThe AI / operational-strategic framework is being moved to a separate dedicated chat.\n\nCURRENT MOMENT\n\nDate: Tuesday, September 8, 2026\n\nDon is closing out the current Airbnb / lodging setup in Las Vegas.\n\nImmediate sequence:\n\npersonal closeout → 10:00 AM interview → 11:00 AM checkout → move to Excalibur → establish better TV/Wi-Fi/work setup\n\nExcalibur is expected to provide a better physical work setup, including TV/display arrangement and hopefully better internet stability.\n\nDo not overload the period before the interview with unnecessary planning.\n\nPERSONAL OPERATING PRIORITIES\n\nKeep the personal lane organized into these buckets:\n\n1. Immediate Vegas logistics\n\n* Interview at 10:00 AM.\n* Checkout around 11:00 AM.\n* Move to Excalibur.\n* Re-establish laptop / Wi-Fi / display / charging setup after arrival.\n* Handle hotel, food, transportation, cash, and reservation issues only as actually needed.\n\n2. Money / liquidity\nMaintain conservative cash-flow discipline.\n\nRules:\n\n* Do not count future income until received.\n* Do not treat casino promotional value as cash.\n* Hotel holds are earmarked liquidity, not spendable money.\n* Protect food, transportation, communications, lodging, and work-enablement first.\n\n3. Career / interviews\nCareer has its own working lane/artifacts, but personal logistics should support it.\n\nCurrent highest-value long-term opportunity remains Myers-Holum, with RF-SMART behind it and other opportunities evaluated on fit rather than activity.\n\nToday’s 10:00 interview is primarily a professional-relationship obligation unless new information materially changes its attractiveness.\n\nDo not turn this personal chat into full job-search operations unless needed for immediate scheduling/logistics.\n\n4. Playa del Karma / family relocation\nThis remains a major personal program.\n\nCurrent direction:\n\n* Family move targeted within the next several months / by roughly December.\n* Playa selected as the family base.\n* Apartment target has evolved toward a good 2–3BR family/work setup rather than a temporary tourist apartment.\n* Desired area is approximately around 15th Avenue / central Playa rather than directly on 5th.\n* Real kitchen/stove, reliable internet, office space, room for son/family growth, and livability matter more than flashy amenities.\n* Landing concept remains short-term neighborhood testing first, then lease.\n* Daphne is a potential relocation / apartment-search operating partner.\n* Jason is useful current-ground-truth context.\n* This is a 5–10 year family strategy: rent first, likely around two years, then evaluate purchasing a condo/home base.\n\nKeep Playa planning practical:\nhousing → family landing → work infrastructure → legal/immigration → budget → neighborhood testing → long-term ownership\n\n5. Family\nFamily/homecoming is the center of the broader personal plan.\n\nDon’s wife and son are currently in Mexico while Don is handling work/career/logistics in the U.S.\n\nRecent movie/personal discussion reinforced the simple emotional anchor:\n\nmake it home\n\nDo not over-psychologize that. It is context, not a task framework.\n\n6. Personal context / craft\nPersonal chronology and personality artifacts already exist in Google Drive.\n\nUseful recurring patterns captured:\n\n* craft over spotlight\n* meaning over structure\n* patience over impulse\n* earned payoff over spectacle\n* authenticity over imitation\n* create the read, then break the read\n* control the game state rather than blindly following the meta\n* infrastructure should reveal skill rather than mask it\n\nGaming, music, movies, storytelling, family, and personal history belong in this lane when relevant.\n\nThey are not GCE doctrine unless Don explicitly promotes something into that framework.\n\n7. Personal AI / mobile execution assistant\nEarly concept only.\n\nDon wants a phone-first personal execution assistant eventually:\n\nvoice command → intent → deterministic execution → short confirmation\n\nPrimary purposes:\n\n* reminders\n* calendar\n* notes\n* tasks\n* small/macro events\n* simple messaging\n* personal execution while walking/traveling/working\n\nThink “voice-controlled personal execution layer,” not chatbot companion.\n\niPhone and Android approaches should both be evaluated later.\n\nThis is not a current build priority this morning.\n\nWORKING STYLE FOR THIS CHAT\n\nDon tends to think rapidly and open multiple personal loops while moving around.\n\nHelp by:\n\n* sorting thoughts into existing buckets\n* closing loops\n* distinguishing NOW / LATER / PARKED\n* avoiding unnecessary new projects\n* preserving anchors\n* asking only questions that materially affect execution\n\nDo not make everything into a framework.\n\nDo not force every insight into an artifact.\n\nKeep responses direct, conversational, and operational.\n\nTODAY — BEFORE OPENING ANY NEW ANALYSIS\n\nFirst establish only:\n\n1. Did the 10:00 interview happen and did anything materially change?\n2. Did checkout/move to Excalibur complete?\n3. What is the actual Wi-Fi / workstation condition after arrival?\n4. Any material cash, reservation, family, or job messages since this handoff?\n5. What personal item actually needs attention next?\n\nEverything else can wait.\n\nCURRENT PERSONAL OPEN ITEMS\n\n* Complete interview.\n* Checkout and move to Excalibur.\n* Establish reliable work environment.\n* Continue Playa del Karma planning later.\n* Review/follow up with Daphne when useful.\n* Maintain conservative Vegas cash-flow / hotel plan.\n* Personal mobile AI assistant remains a future POC/design item.\n* Continue separating personal, career, and GCE/framework chats rather than allowing one giant conversation to become the source of every operating lane.\n\nSESSION START RULE\n\nDo not reconstruct Don’s entire biography or planning history.\n\nStart from the current operating state above and update only what changed.\n\nSTATUS: PROCEED\nCONFIDENCE: 97%\nOUTCOME: personal lane isolated and ready for continuation\nOPEN ITEMS: interview · Excalibur move · work setup · Playa/family follow-ups · personal execution assistant later\nNEXT ROUTE: immediate personal morning execution\nDON INPUT NEEDED: only real-world changes since this handoff\n\nThat should give the new personal chat everything it needs without dragging the AI organization into it. The second handoff later can be pure GCE / AI-stack operational-strategic state.", "start_idx": 0, "title": "Check interview backup", "type": "grouped_webpages", "url": "https://chatgpt.com/c/6aa02a89-f23c-83e8-8a70-8dccdb3c79f3"}, "citation_uuid": "cd20c9a6-617e-4bb7-af83-f1ba7b5eccb5", "deleted": false, "feedback": null, "retrieval_origin": "pca"}, {"citation": {"alt": "", "attribution": "Past chat", "category": "memory", "end_idx": 0, "matched_text": "", "prompt_text": null, "pub_date": 1788124043.093, "refs": [], "retrieval_origin": "pca", "snippet": "Hey, I need a simple prompt. To audit all subfolders. And catalog them. Catalog them. By just folder name, type, and last used. An AI agent. ", "start_idx": 0, "title": "Vdara close out - froze ", "type": "grouped_webpages", "url": "https://chatgpt.com/c/6a949b6e-bcf0-83e8-9105-eca4a47db58e"}, "citation_uuid": "5342061b-bb50-4cf1-b4ff-9efd11280a20", "deleted": false, "feedback": null, "retrieval_origin": "pca"}, {"citation": {"alt": "", "attribution": "Past chat", "category": "memory", "end_idx": 0, "matched_text": "", "prompt_text": null, "pub_date": 1789066878.640336, "refs": [], "retrieval_origin": "pca", "snippet": "Go ahead and pull up everything from the Vegas budget to entertainment and food for us to go and reconcile the next two weeks because we are officially at New York New York on September 10 checked in and we’ll go through everything quickly. We don’t want to spend hours on this so ground yourself get the framework get the files and artifacts.", "start_idx": 0, "title": "Reconcile Vegas Budget", "type": "grouped_webpages", "url": "https://chatgpt.com/c/6aa2fe5a-2e74-83e8-8734-bc12b99f19c5"}, "citation_uuid": "3f72d36e-25ca-4fef-80dc-9195e749a679", "deleted": false, "feedback": null, "retrieval_origin": "pca"}, {"citation": {"alt": "", "attribution": "Past chat", "category": "memory", "end_idx": 0, "matched_text": "", "prompt_text": null, "pub_date": 1788980766.654329, "refs": [], "retrieval_origin": "pca", "snippet": "The conversation below is an SRT transcript. Based on the transcript, provide the assistant response to the latest user turn. Do not end your turn with only an acknowledgment, status update, or filler such as saying you are checking. If you start with a brief acknowledgment, continue until you have either made concrete progress on the user's request or produced a substantive follow-up message. If the latest user turn asks for current information or search-backed facts, use the available tools before ending your turn.\n\nThe current date is Wednesday, September 9, 2026. The time at the start of the call is 12:04 PM. The user's timezone is America/Los_Angeles.\n\n1\n00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,200\nassistant: I don’t see the Marshalls sock-photo sequence in this current chat.\nWhat I can confirm is that you’d already had **socks and underwear on the cheap-shopping list** for Ross/Marshalls-type stores, but I can’t verify from this thread that you sent me a bunch of Marshalls sock pictures here.\nSo if you’re looking for **the chat where you actually showed me the socks**, it’s probably a different one. memcite\n\n2\n00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:00,400\nassistant: Worked for 6s\n\n3\n00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:00,600\nassistant: Yep — now I see the Marshalls sock batch.\nFor **your use case — big flat feet + miles of Vegas walking + current shoes not giving you enough cushioning** — I’d rank these:\n1. **Prince cushioned crew, $7.99 / 3-pack** — best-looking option here for actual walking. It explicitly says **cushioned footbed + moisture wicking + cotton blend**. That’s what I care about most for you right now.\n2. **Puma** — probably my second choice if the package confirms full-foot cushioning and the size is right. Puma athletic socks are generally a safer walking choice than gimmicky “copper” socks.\n3. **The 6-pair cushioned ankle, $7.99** — excellent value, but I’d physically squeeze the heel and forefoot. If the cushion is substantial, this could actually win on value.\n4. **Copper Sole Athletic Sport** — I’d put this last. “Copper yarn” is not the thing solving your problem. Cushioning, fit, sweat management, and avoiding rubbing are.\n**Biggest filter before price:** check the shoe-size range. If you’re outside the stated range, don’t buy them just because they’re cheap. A sock stretched too tight across a large flat foot can actually make a long walk feel worse.\nIf you’re standing there right now, **send me the back of the Prince and Puma packages with the size/material/cushion details**, and I’ll pick one immediately.\n\n4\n00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:00,800\nuser [text]: Yeah, I think that’s what you said last time too. I’m gonna go with the three pack cause that works.\n\n5\n00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:01,000\nassistant: Worked for a couple of seconds\n\n6\n00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:01,200\nassistant: Yep — the **Prince 3-pack** is the clean pick.\nFor $7.99 you’re getting the combination you actually need: **cushioned footbed, moisture wicking, cotton blend, crew height**. For all the walking you’re doing, that matters more than getting six thinner pairs.\nI’d take those and close the sock loop.\n\n7\n00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:01,400\nassistant: Worked for 5s\n\n8\n00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:01,600\nassistant: Bam. This gives us the answer.\n**Myers-Holum = green light. You’re moving forward.** The leadership discussion did **not** produce a no-go, and they are not parking you. Jillian explicitly says:\n> “We’re excited to move forward with the interview process.”\nThe important wording is **“next interview(s)”** and **“next steps.”** So this is **not an offer yet**, and it also doesn’t tell us wh