tribution": "www.usmobile.com", "pub_date": null, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 13, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 609988}, "snippet": "", "title": "Starter Kit", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://www.usmobile.com/shop/product/starter-kit/starter-kit-sim"}], "type": "search_result_group"}, {"domain": "www.att.com", "entries": [{"attribution": "www.att.com", "pub_date": null, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 5, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 609988}, "snippet": "", "title": "Prepaid International Data Plan: Roaming & Call Rates | AT&T", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://www.att.com/prepaid/international-calling/"}, {"attribution": "www.att.com", "pub_date": null, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 6, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 609988}, "snippet": "", "title": "Plan de datos internacionales prepagado: tarifas de roaming y llamadas | AT&T", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://www.att.com/es-us/prepaid/international-calling/"}, {"attribution": "www.att.com", "pub_date": null, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 11, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 609988}, "snippet": "", "title": "Planes de teléfono 5G prepagados: teléfonos 5G, tarjetas SIM y Wi-Fi | AT&T", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://www.att.com/es-us/prepaid/5g/"}], "type": "search_result_group"}], "thinking_effort": "standard", "tool_icons": ["https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.att.com&sz=128"], "turn_exchange_id": "76e9a305-b3b1-4ef7-8a82-73b301836091", "turn_id": "2143a89c-4cf8-4945-a7d2-f593ca293d12", "working_turn_id": "76e9a305-b3b1-4ef7-8a82-73b301836091"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yes — you absolutely have viable **$25–$45/month** options that fit the U.S./Mexico + eSIM + BYO Android model. I’d structure this as a decision tree:\n\n- **First choice: T-Mobile Keep & Switch**, because if Spectrum qualifies and your phone/device-financing paperwork clears, T-Mobile can reimburse up to **$800 per line** via virtual prepaid Mastercard after you port and submit proof. T-Mobile says the device financing must generally be at least 90 days old with at least three successful minimum payments, and the reimbursement typically takes about 15 days after submission. citeturn664719search0turn664719search4\n- **If T-Mobile falls through: Visible+ is probably the cleanest fit for your use case.** Current promo pricing is **$29/month**, taxes/fees included, with unlimited talk/text/data in Mexico and Canada and **2 GB of high-speed data per day** while roaming there, then reduced speeds. Visible+ Pro is **$39/month** with more perks, but you probably don’t need it. citeturn664719search5\n- **US Mobile is the flexibility play.** Unlimited Starter is **$25/month** taxes/fees included, but monthly Starter does **not** include the same meaningful Mexico roaming bucket by default; you can add roaming, or use their North America by-the-gig setup. Their Premium plan gives up to **20 GB international roaming** and costs more. US Mobile also supports eSIM and multiple underlying networks, which is nice if you want carrier flexibility. citeturn609988search7turn609988search8turn664719search1\n- **AT&T Prepaid is the boring but solid fallback.** Their current **Unlimited Enhanced Plus is $45/month** and explicitly includes Mexico and Canada use, with unlimited talk/text/data and 10 GB hotspot. citeturn609988search5\n- **Google Fi works well internationally, but it misses your price target for one line.** Unlimited Premium is **$65/month** and gives broad international coverage; Unlimited Standard has Canada/Mexico support but is priced better mostly when you have multiple lines. citeturn664719search6\n\nFor what you actually described — **one line, U.S. + Mexico, eSIM, Android, solid data, around $40 or less** — I’d narrow it to:\n\n**1. T-Mobile**, if they pay off Spectrum.  \n**2. Visible+ at ~$29**, if you want the simplest low-cost U.S./Mexico setup.  \n**3. US Mobile**, if you want more control over network choice and roaming configuration.  \n**4. AT&T Prepaid at $45**, if you want mainstream-carrier simplicity and don’t mind being slightly above target.\n\nAnd because you’re planning to spend real time in Playa, one technical point matters: **Mexico roaming terms are often built for travel, not permanent majority-of-use in Mexico.** So before we lock anything, we should specifically check each carrier’s long-term roaming/fair-use rule. That’s the next thing I’d compare, because it matters more for you than headline price. citeturn664719search7\n\nIf you want, I can do the next pass specifically as **“best plan for living in Mexico but keeping a U.S. number”** and strip out anything that’s really only good for short trips."]}, "create_time": 1789836669.785363, "end_turn": true, "id": "a78bbdea-899b-4585-95eb-3711f17a25f6", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [{"alt": "([T-Mobile](https://www.t-mobile.com/support/new-to-tmobile/keep-and-switch?utm_source=chatgpt.com))", "end_idx": 622, "error": null, "fallback_items": null, "items": [{"attribution": "T-Mobile", "attribution_segments": null, "attributions": null, "hue": null, "pub_date": null, "refs": [{"ref_index": 0, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}, {"ref_index": 4, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}], "snippet": "", "supporting_websites": [{"attribution": "T-Mobile", "pub_date": null, "snippet": "", "title": "Switch to T-Mobile from Verizon or AT&T & Bring Your Phone", "url": "https://www.t-mobile.com/switch/keep-phone-switch-from-verizon-or-att?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}], "title": "Keep and Switch | T-Mobile Support: Help with Devices, Plans, Billing & More", "url": "https://www.t-mobile.com/support/new-to-tmobile/keep-and-switch?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}], "matched_text": "citeturn664719search0