 "snippet": "", "title": "OnePlus 12R Specs - OnePlus (Slovensko)", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://www.oneplus.com/sk/12r/specs"}, {"attribution": "www.oneplus.com", "pub_date": null, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 10, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 651007}, "snippet": "", "title": "OnePlus 12R Genshin Impact Edition Specs - OnePlus (Česká Republika)", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://www.oneplus.com/cz/12r-edition/specs"}], "type": "search_result_group"}, {"domain": "community.oneplus.com", "entries": [{"attribution": "community.oneplus.com", "pub_date": 1750982400, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 8, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 651007}, "snippet": "", "title": "OxygenOS 15.0.0.831 for the OnePlus 11 [NA ADDED]", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://community.oneplus.com/thread/1892197392460021763"}], "type": "search_result_group"}], "thinking_effort": "standard", "tool_icons": ["https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.samsung.com&sz=128", "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=support.google.com&sz=128", "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=community.oneplus.com&sz=128"], "turn_exchange_id": "4a409f0a-8900-4b8d-837e-d89456a850f3", "turn_id": "c09d158a-85b7-41a6-abd4-acba77a5541f", "working_turn_id": "4a409f0a-8900-4b8d-837e-d89456a850f3"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yeah — with a hard **$100 pawn-shop target**, I would not make OnePlus the only target. The eSIM requirement narrows the field a lot, and older OnePlus support is inconsistent. For example, the **OnePlus 12R does not support eSIM** on the official spec page, so we need to verify exact model numbers before buying. citeturn651007search7turn651007search10\n\nThe cleaner used-phone targets are:\n\n| Phone | Why it fits | Pawn target |\n|---|---|---:|\n| **Google Pixel 6a** | eSIM + physical SIM, 5G, broad U.S./Mexico bands, Wi-Fi 6E | **$80–120** |\n| **Google Pixel 7** | newer, better modem/camera, eSIM + physical SIM | **$120–170** |\n| **OnePlus 11 5G** | Snapdragon 8 Gen 2, still current enough for OxygenOS 16, strong performance | **$150–220** |\n| **Samsung S22** | Snapdragon in U.S. model, eSIM support, strong carrier compatibility | **$140–200** |\n| **Samsung S23 FE / S23** | better long-term support, eSIM, strong U.S./Mexico carrier fit | **$180–250** |\n\nFor **$100 specifically**, the **Pixel 6a is probably the sweet spot**. Google confirms it supports **dual SIM with nano-SIM + eSIM**, and the U.S. model has a broad LTE/5G band set including bands useful on U.S. networks and Mexico. citeturn651007search1turn651007search2\n\nThe OnePlus route is still good if you find the right one. I’d target a **OnePlus 11 5G, North American model CPH2451**, because that model is still getting current OxygenOS updates. citeturn651007search8 I would **not buy any OnePlus at a pawn shop until we confirm the exact model number and eSIM menu**.\n\nFor your service, since you said **10 GB/month is enough**, you do not necessarily need an expensive unlimited plan. A few workable structures are:\n\n- **AT&T Prepaid 8 GB / 3-month plan:** about **$33/month**, and it explicitly works in the **U.S., Mexico, and Canada** with the same 8 GB bucket. After 8 GB, speeds drop to 128 Kbps. citeturn242784search9\n- **AT&T Prepaid Unlimited Enhanced Plus:** **$45/month**, Mexico/Canada included, unlimited domestic data and 10 GB hotspot. citeturn242784search8\n- **Visible:** starts around **$25/month** for unlimited U.S. data, but I would only use it for your Mexico plan after confirming the exact roaming tier and IMEI compatibility. Visible explicitly warns that not every BYOD Android works on its network, so we need to run the pawn-shop IMEI before buying. citeturn242784search4turn242784search10\n- **US Mobile:** flexible, but Mexico roaming on the cheaper tiers is more piecemeal; their add-ons are **$15 for 1 GB** or **$30 for 5 GB**, while Premium includes much more international roaming. citeturn242784search1turn242784search3\n\nFor your exact use case, I’d hunt in this order: **Pixel 6a first, Pixel 7 second, OnePlus 11 if we get lucky, Samsung S22 as another strong fallback.**\n\nAt the pawn shop, before handing them a dollar, check four things: **unlocked, clean IMEI, EID present under `*#06#`, and battery/USB-C condition**. AT&T specifically says an **EID** is the quick confirmation that the device can use eSIM. citeturn242784search5\n\nIf you send me photos/model numbers from the pawn shop, I can tell you **buy / pass** on each one in real time."]}, "create_time": 1789836727.136239, "end_turn": true, "id": "d1a768ad-e3c8-403c-82ea-d0822346a58e", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [{"alt": "([OnePlus](https://www.oneplus.com/sk/12r/specs?utm_source=chatgpt.com))", "end_idx": 358, "error": null, "fallback_items": null, "items": [{"attribution": "OnePlus", "attribution_segments": null, "attributions": null, "hue": null, "pub_date": null, "refs": [{"ref_index": 7, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 1}, {"ref_index": 10, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 1}], "snippet": "", "supporting_websites": [{"attribution": "OnePlus", "pub_date": null, "snippet": "", "title": "OnePlus 12R Genshin Impact Edition Specs - OnePlus (Česká Republika)", "url": "https://www.oneplus.com/cz/12r-edition/specs?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}], "title": "OnePlus 12R Specs - OnePlus (Slovensko)", "url": "https://www.oneplus.com/sk/12r/specs?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}], "matched_text": "citeturn651007search7turn651007search10", "prefix": null, "prompt_text": null, "refs": [], "safe_urls": ["https://www.oneplus.com/cz/12r-edition/specs", "https://www.oneplus.com/cz/12r-edition/specs?utm_source=chatgpt.com", "https://www.oneplus.com/sk/12r/specs", "https://www.on