nal-gdrive:account:112404107312407557615:file:1ZRwkt2RPOAbbecosfWzENp2QdI_z71kLMrOzE0HX0D4\",\"version_id\":null,\"file_provider\":\"google_drive\",\"name\":\"Vegas Food, Exercise, and Daily Rhythm — Living Plan.docx\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document\",\"surface\":\"library\",\"mode\":\"full\",\"include_text\":true,\"include_images\":false,\"requested_start_page\":null,\"requested_end_page\":null,\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":100,\"total_lines\":100,\"has_more\":false,\"next_start_line\":null,\"next_start_page\":null,\"next_read\":null,\"next_image_read\":null,\"pages\":[],\"num_pages\":0,\"created_at\":null,\"modified_at\":null,\"size_bytes\":12425,\"content\":[\"\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nVegas Food, Exercise, and Daily Rhythm — Living Plan\\nCurrent as of Sep 2, 2026. Update whenever prices, credits, appetite, energy, or travel conditions change.\\nPurpose\\n· Build a sustainable food, exercise, focus, and recovery rhythm without destabilizing hotel liquidity.\\n· Use comp credits, groceries, and properly timed value meals as planned tools rather than surprise spending.\\n· The structure is a simple breakfast plus one satiating anchor meal, with hydration or additional food adjusted to actual energy and health needs.\\nCurrent food bridge\\n· Sep 2, 2026 — Late buffet lunch and snacks were charged to the Excalibur room. Approximately $50 is now expected back from the $150 hold after the known charges. There was no immediate cash out, but the final checkout folio controls the actual refund.\\n· Sep 3, 2026 — Whole Foods groceries planned: eggs and other simple breakfast basics. Actual total is TBD; prioritize items that cover several breakfasts.\\n· This weekend — Chinatown Chinese buffet target: approximately $20-something, used at the appropriate time as the filling main meal. Confirm the current price, hours, and transportation cost before going.\\n· First Vdara stay — $150 eligible food credit. No minibar. Use the credit deliberately for filling food and only eligible, purposeful room charges.\\nBudget method\\n· Use hotel credits and comps first, groceries second, and value meals third.\\n· A room charge is deferred settlement, not free spending. Reduce the expected refund or add the amount due as soon as the folio is known.\\n· Track cash food spending as B. Update B only from actual receipts or posted folio charges.\\n· Avoid minibar and hotel convenience pricing for water, detergent, deodorant, alcohol, snacks, and ordinary supplies.\\n· Choose a satisfying anchor meal at the right time instead of scattered purchases that cost more and provide less food.\\nExercise and recovery\\n· Use walking as the default movement and transportation option when practical; the current comfortable range is approximately two to three miles.\\n· Use bodyweight exercise, hotel fitness facilities, swimming, or a structured walk as no-cost decompression.\\n· Excalibur blocks remain focused work periods with minimal paid entertainment. Exercise supplies the release without touching the budget.\\n· Vdara blocks provide the controlled comp-funded recovery window through food credit and free play.\\nDaily rhythm\\n· Simple grocery breakfast.\\n· Focused job-search and AI-framework work block.\\n· One properly timed, filling anchor meal.\\n· Walking or a short workout.\\n· Low-cost or comp-funded decompression, then reassess the next lodging and cash checkpoint.\\nOpen variables\\n· Final Excalibur folio and confirmation that approximately $50 returns from the $150 hold after the buffet, snacks, room balance, and other known room charges.\\n· Actual Whole Foods grocery total and how many breakfasts it covers.\\n· Confirmed Chinatown buffet price, hours, and transportation cost.\\n· Cash food requirement after credits are exhausted.\\n· Any adjustment required by hunger, energy, sleep, workload, or health.\\n\\nSeptember 3, 2026 — Current food/liquidity rule\\n* The current Excalibur incidental authorization is being treated as substantially consumed by necessary food charges rather than preserved for a small refund.\\n* Today’s TAP meal is a practical closeout meal; eating now takes priority over preserving a hypothetical small residual authorization refund.\\n* Future hotel-food strategy: groceries and ordinary meals should generally stay off the room folio when hotel-hold liquidity needs to recycle into the next stay.\\n* True comp food credits remain useful and should be used deliberately; minibar and ordinary room charges should be avoided during liquidity-sensitive stays.\\n* The next clean-hold stay will be used to observe actual authorization-release timing without incidental folio reconciliation\\nSeptember 3, 2026 — Standing core breakfast / meal system\\n* Current hard grocery budget: $48.02.\\n* Core purchase list, in order: protein powder; five avocados; chia or chia/flax/hemp seed blend; Neuro Mints; cheese or eggs; small electrolyte packets only if they fit the remaining budget.\\n* Protein powder: observed Whole Foods price $28.80. This is the known shelf price from the current plan and should not be replaced with an estimated target.\\n* Avocados: five total. Observed pricing was about 3 for $5; confirm the actual per-unit/promo price at purchase.\\n* Chia / seed blend: standing nutrition staple. Prior observed 365 Super Seed Trio price was about $8.69.\\n* Neuro Mints: standing low-dose focus item; prior working price was about $3.\\n* Cheese or eggs: choose the better-value whole-food protein/fat option at the shelf price. Seek a cheaper cheese option than the earlier roughly $4 target when available.\\n* Tuna is removed from the standing core cart for now. It can return later as an optional protein item, but it does not get priority inside the current $48.02 cap.\\n* Small electrolyte packets were observed around $0.78 each; buy only a few and only after the core food items fit.\\n* This is the default hotel grocery template: compact protein + avocado + seeds + one whole-food protein/fat item, with hydration/focus support layered in only when the budget allows.\\n* Ordinary hotel food is avoided unless a true food credit covers it. The goal is to make this repeatable beyond the current two-day pinch, not to build a one-off emergency cart.\\nSeptember 4, 2026 — tomorrow grocery execution / standing meal rhythm\\n* Hard grocery budget remains $48.02. Do not substitute estimates for observed prices.\\n* Whole Foods observed core prices: 365 protein powder $28.80; 365 Super Seed Trio/chia-flax-hemp blend about $8.69; Neuro Mints about $3; small electrolyte packets about $0.78 each.\\n* Five avocados are part of the standing cart. Prior promo observation was about 3 for $5; use the actual shelf/promo price tomorrow rather than inventing a number.\\n* Cheese or eggs fills the remaining whole-food protein/fat slot based on actual shelf price. Find the cheaper practical cheese/egg option rather than forcing a preset estimate.\\n* Tuna is not part of tomorrow’s Whole Foods core cart. It can be bought later in Chinatown/another market if a materially cheaper can is found.\\n* Nutrition rhythm: morning can be avocado + eggs + protein shake. If work/interviews prevent leaving, use the remaining avocado + cheese/eggs + another protein shake as the second buffer meal. Then add one inexpensive real meal later in the day or use a genuine buffet/food credit.\\n* Purpose of the protein powder outlay: portable multi-day meal support and interview-day insurance. It is intended to prevent hunger-driven $20–$50 hotel/gift-shop purchases, not replace all whole food.\\n* Current hotel-food lesson: roughly $50/day of random Excalibur food over several days is the leakage this system is designed to stop. Groceries create a repeatable baseline; hotel food is used only when covered by a true credit or when no reasonable alternative exists.\\n* Weekend support: Palms $50 buffet credit and approximately $20–$25 Chinatown buffet options can serve as planned anchor meals, while the grocery kit covers breakfast/workday hunger and keeps room charges off the folio.\\n* Tomorrow execution: go directly to the known Whole Foods items; no wandering or rebuilding the list in-store. Buy the known core first, then use only the remaining dollars for avocados, cheese/eggs, and a few electrolyte packets according to actual shelf prices.\\n\\n\\n\\nSeptember 4, 2026 — Whole Foods execution result / standing grocery baseline\\n* Actual Whole Foods operating basket was built from observed shelf prices, not estimates.\\n* 4 avocados — $5.00 total.\\n* 365 Super Seed Trio — $8.69.\\n* Neuro Mints — $3.07.\\n* 2 electrolyte sticks — $0.78 each / $1.56 total.\\n* 365 Sharp Cheddar, 8 oz — $2.99.\\n* 365 Organic Pea Protein — $11.38. This replaced the $28.80 whey for the immediate bridge because it preserved cash while still supplying portable protein.\\n* Sedona sparkling water — $3.19.\\n* Identified line-item subtotal is $35.88 before tax/any checkout difference; user reported the actual grocery outlay as approximately $38. Use the posted receipt/SoFi transaction as final B when available.\\n* Amazon gift-card balance could not be used in Whole Foods in-store checkout. Approximately $48 remains online for Amazon/Locker use. Reserve it first for shelf-stable sardines and electrolyte replenishment; add only other essential Locker-eligible groceries that fit the remaining balance. This is restricted purchasing power, not cash and not Whole Foods spending capacity.\\n* Eggs were intentionally deferred to the cheaper market near the Airbnb because carrying eggs during the transition is impractical and local dozen pricing around $3.99 was observed as better value than prepared hard-boiled eggs.\\n* Tuna and beef broth were intentionally deferred. Tuna can be sourced more cheaply in Chinatown/99 Ranch/SF Supermarket; beef broth is optional and not required for the core system.\\n* Core meal rhythm remains: protein + avocado + seed blend, with cheese/eggs as the whole-food add-on; use a second small buffer meal during work/interviews if needed, then one inexpensive real meal later. Objective is to eliminate repeated $30–$50 hotel/gift-shop food leakage without starving or forcing three restaurant meals per day.\\n* Replenishment rule: buy only when the current core is running low. Future electrolyte bulk products, creatine/electrolyte combinations, moringa/matcha, or larger protein tubs remain future-stack options, not immediate purchases\\nCURRENT FOOD / CASH POSITION\\n· Whole Foods baseline is already purchased at approximately $38 cash. The remaining Amazon gift-card balance is restricted online purchasing power, not food cash.\\n· Use the grocery kit first: pea protein, avocados, seed blend, cheddar, electrolytes, and eggs when bought at the lower-cost market. Replenish only when the current core is running low.\\n· Free-food offers can be used deliberately. A Sonic free burger with a $2 slush counts as only the actual $2 cash spend; do not add paid extras.\\n· During the next Excalibur block, keep ordinary food off the room folio. The food goal is satiation and stable work energy, not a new restaurant budget.\\n· Next food gate: protect the current grocery kit through the Airbnb bridge. Excalibur is shortened; jewelry proceeds remain unavailable. Avoid unplanned food spending while Tuesday’s incidental hold and actual unemployment posting remain pending.\\n.\\n\"],\"warnings\":[],\"cloud_doc_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZRwkt2RPOAbbecosfWzENp2QdI_z71kLMrOzE0HX0D4\"}],\"warnings\":[]}"}, "create_time": 1790016732.3850148, "end_turn": null, "id": "d7257eec-3f1b-43a2-b2be-1aa7b097c60a", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "chime_version": 1, "classifier_response": "default", "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "invoked_plugin": {}, "invoked_resource": {"api_tool_version": "v2", "contains_mcp_source": false, "description": "Re