loseout request\n\n**PRIMARY AUTHORITY:** Don  \n**PRIMARY SEATS INVOLVED:** Don; Coda  \n**CURRENT STATUS:** **HANDOFF REQUIRED**  \n**CONFIDENCE:** **97%**\n\n---\n\n# 2. WHAT THIS CHAT WAS ACTUALLY ABOUT\n\n### Original objective\nThe chat functioned as a live personal operating lane for surviving and stabilizing the Vegas period: hotel sequencing, authorization holds, available cash, incoming money, food credits, free play, computer/phone issues, and job-transition implications.\n\n### Major pivots\nThe workstream progressively narrowed from reactive day-to-day liquidity management into three durable outcomes:\n\n1. **Freeze the Vegas hotel calendar and cash-flow ledger** so it would stop being re-derived.\n2. Treat larger hotel holds, especially **Vdara**, as an intentional **forced-savings / liquidity-protection mechanism**, not merely a burden.\n3. Split **health/wellness** and the potential **Orlando/ATEX transition** into separate lanes instead of letting them contaminate the Vegas operating ledger.\n\n### Final scope\nBy the end, this chat was no longer for active optimization. It became a **closeout and handoff source** for:\n- frozen Vegas hotel/cash-flow state;\n- the rationale behind the larger holds;\n- the boundary between Vegas liquidity and Orlando transition costs;\n- a separate health/wellness handoff based on the relevant Google Drive material.\n\n---\n\n# 3. ACCOMPLISHMENTS BY DATE\n\n## DATE: 2026-09-20\n**WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** Luxor stay was closed operationally with resort-credit usage and clean-folio behavior validated.  \n**DECISION / RESULT:** The Luxor $300 resort credit was essentially exhausted, leaving approximately **$4.68**. Clean folio strategy was confirmed as the desired mechanism for fast authorization recycling.  \n**WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Don operationally; Coda reconciliation.  \n**STATUS:** **verified**\n\n## DATE: 2026-09-20\n**WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** The cash-flow model was corrected after several mistaken re-der